#: includes/configs/settings.php:34
msgid "Address Display"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:35
msgid "Locations are usually saved in full, such as \"Edinburgh, Scotland, United Kingdom\". These settings shorten what visitors see. What is already stored is left alone, so you can switch back at any time and nothing has to be re-entered, unless you tick the last setting in this section, which shortens new entries as they are saved."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:40
msgid "Address Format"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:41
msgid "Choose how much of each saved address to show. Addresses are split on commas, so \"Edinburgh, Scotland, United Kingdom\" has three parts, counted from the left. A theme that supplies its own address markup keeps it, so this has no effect on ExpertHive, JobHive or MeetingHive."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:47
msgid "Full address"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:48
msgid "First part only (Edinburgh)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:49
msgid "First two parts (Edinburgh, Scotland)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:50
msgid "First and last parts (Edinburgh, United Kingdom)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:51
msgid "Everything except the last part (Edinburgh, Scotland)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:52
msgid "Last part only (United Kingdom)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:53
msgid "A set number of parts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:58
msgid "Number of Parts (used with \"A set number of parts\")"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:59
msgid "How many comma separated parts to show, counted from the left. Only used when the format above is set to a set number of parts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:68
msgid "Saved Value"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:69
msgid "By default the full address is saved and only shortened when it is displayed. Tick this to shorten it as people pick a suggestion, so the short version is what gets saved. Existing entries are not changed. This applies to every location attribute you create, on any map provider, and to the built-in location field when one of the providers this plugin adds is selected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:70
msgid "Save the shortened address instead"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:78
msgid "Location Suggestions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:79
msgid "Controls the list of places that drops down while somebody types in a location field. Restricting it is the tidiest way to keep every saved location consistent, because people can no longer pick a street address when you wanted a city."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:84
msgid "Suggestion Types"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:85
msgid "Select the kinds of place people are allowed to choose. Leave this empty to allow everything, which is the standard behaviour. This applies to the location field a listing is filed and searched by, and not to the Location attributes you create yourself, which keep offering everything so that a field named for an address can still accept one. The extension setting \"Hide the exact address\" behaves the same way: it shortens the listing location and leaves your attributes alone. Geocoders vary in how strictly they honour this, so a few unexpected results can still appear."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:92
msgid "Country"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:93
msgid "Region"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:94
msgid "Subregion"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:95
msgid "City"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:96
msgid "District"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:97
msgid "Postcode"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:98
msgid "Street address"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:103
msgid "Minimum Length (characters)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:104
msgid "How many characters somebody must type before suggestions are requested. Raising this cuts the number of requests your geocoder receives, which matters on the free plans. Google Maps and Mapbox run their own suggestion box and ignore this, so it applies to the location attributes you create and, when one of the providers this plugin adds is selected, to the built-in location field as well."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:116
msgid "Map Appearance"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:117
msgid "Applies to maps drawn by the map providers this plugin adds. Google Maps and Mapbox draw their own maps and are not affected by these settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:122
msgid "Map Style"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:123
msgid "The look of the map itself. The choices change depending on which map provider is selected above, so save the provider first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:131
msgid "Marker Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:132
msgid "The colour of the pins on the map, as a six digit hex code such as #ff5a5f. Leave it empty for the default blue (#3a77ff), which is the marker colour the HivePress Geolocation extension uses on Google Maps."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:141
msgid "Removing the Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:142
msgid "What happens to these settings if you ever delete Geolocation Plus. They are kept by default, so reinstalling restores everything. WordPress will warn you that deleting a plugin also deletes its data whichever way the setting below is left, so ignore that wording and trust this setting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:147
msgid "Deleting the Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:148
msgid "Tick this only if you want the settings removed for good, which cannot be undone. It removes the address, suggestion and map settings on this page, and the MapTiler, Geoapify and LocationIQ API keys in the Integrations section."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:149
msgid "Delete all data when this plugin is deleted"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:163
msgid "Only used when MapTiler is selected as the map provider. Create a free account at maptiler.com, then copy the key from the Keys page of your account. Restrict the key to your own domain in the provider dashboard before you paste it here: it is used in the visitor browser, as these services intend, so it is readable by anyone who views the page and an unrestricted key can be used up by somebody else. Good coverage and seven map styles, the widest choice here. Worth knowing before you choose it: MapTiler has no single \"city\" level in the United Kingdom, so a listing in the middle of a large city can be filed under a named district of it, such as Old Town in Edinburgh. Smaller towns and cities are named as you would expect, and this plugin checks with MapTiler whether a county is also a city so that places like Cardiff and Nottingham come out right."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:178
msgid "Only used when Geoapify is selected as the map provider. Create a free account at geoapify.com, add a project, then copy the API key it gives you. Restrict the key to your own domain in the provider dashboard before you paste it here: it is used in the visitor browser, as these services intend, so it is readable by anyone who views the page and an unrestricted key can be used up by somebody else. Names places consistently and handles cities well. It writes some labels its own way, abbreviating England to \"ENG\" and occasionally beginning a building result with \"yes\", which comes from the underlying map data rather than from this plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:193
msgid "Only used when LocationIQ is selected as the map provider. Create a free account at locationiq.com, then copy the access token from the Dashboard. Restrict the key to your own domain in the provider dashboard before you paste it here: it is used in the visitor browser, as these services intend, so it is readable by anyone who views the page and an unrestricted key can be used up by somebody else. The most detailed addresses of the three, often naming the neighbourhood as well as the town. Its free plan allows about one search a second, which is ample for typing but can be reached by automated tools. It sometimes names a city by its council area, such as \"Aberdeen City\" rather than \"Aberdeen\", so a site that has already built region pages under another provider may end up with both."
msgstr ""

